$$
\det(\lambda I-A)=0,
$$
so $\lambda I-A$ has a nonzero kernel. Any nonzero $v$ in that kernel satisfies
$$
Av=\lambda v.
$$
Thus $\lambda$ is an <eigenvalue> and $v$ is a corresponding <eigenvector>.

