The integrating factor is $e^{t^3}$, so
$$
\frac d{dt}(e^{t^3}z)=t.
$$
Hence
$$
e^{t^3}\sqrt{x}=\frac{t^2}{2}+C.
$$
The condition $x(1)=4$ gives $C=2e-\tfrac12$. Consequently
$$
