=n^{\,1-\alpha c(n-1)/n}
\longrightarrow\infty.
$$
Also $p\to0$, so both terms in the variance ratio tend to zero. Part (iv) now applies and proves the lower side of the isolated-vertex threshold:
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P(N=0)\longrightarrow0}.
