$$
has at most $s(H,n)$ distinct members, each with Euclidean norm at most $M\sqrt n$. The <Massart finite-class lemma>, the <Sauer-Shelah growth bound>, and $VC(H)\leq p$ give
$$
\widehat R(\mathcal F)
\leq M\sqrt{\frac{2\log s(H,n)}n}
\leq M\sqrt{\frac{2p\log(n+1)}n}.
$$
Taking expectations and substituting this into part (i) yields
$$
